senses.gloss:
प्रर्क्षीय प्रर्क्षीय (fr. 1. प्र + ऋक्ष),
Nom. P. प्रर्क्षीयति, &c., see Vopa-deva II. 4;
(also प्रार्क्षीय.)

प्रार्थनीय, अस्, आ, अम्, to be desired or wished
for; to be asked or begged; to be prayed for;
worthy of desire, desirable, proper to be solicited;
(अम्), n. the third or Dvāpara age of the world.

प्रार्द् प्रार्द् (प्र-अर्द्), Caus. P. प्रार्दयति,
-यितुम्, Ved. to exert beyond measure, overwork;
to cause to flow away.
